00:21:39.360 --> 00:21:42.000
They operate solely in like Jira and confluence.

488
00:21:42.000 --> 00:21:46.400
So I can't explain to 100 managers go and go make an account on GitHub.

489
00:21:46.400 --> 00:21:48.920
And now you got to put this in confluence.

490
00:21:48.920 --> 00:21:51.240
So there's there's really cool open source tools.

491
00:21:51.240 --> 00:21:54.560
You can build your own script to basically convert that readme

492
00:21:54.560 --> 00:21:57.800
that's in the project directly to just ship that to confluence.

493
00:21:57.840 --> 00:21:58.040
Right.

494
00:21:58.040 --> 00:22:01.280
You make a doc, think hashtag one and markdown becomes H1.

495
00:22:01.520 --> 00:22:04.560
It's a very simple, very deterministic conversion.

496
00:22:04.600 --> 00:22:06.400
Don't have an LLM, just update confluence

497
00:22:06.400 --> 00:22:08.840
I mean you can do that too, but it's kind of token heavy

498
00:22:08.840 --> 00:22:11.200
just to have your agent write a deterministic script to

499
00:22:11.200 --> 00:22:15.320
sync that markdown into a pretty HTML file that everyone in that other system uses.

500
00:22:15.360 --> 00:22:16.960
And that was it. And that was all I did.

501
00:22:16.960 --> 00:22:19.000
So now when someone asked me for, hey,

502
00:22:19.000 --> 00:22:20.960
can you tell me about that agent framework or I,

503
00:22:20.960 --> 00:22:24.880
they just ping me on WebEx and ask me, where can I get information about this?

504
00:22:24.920 --> 00:22:28.720
I send them just a link to that confluence doc, which is a direct

505
00:22:28.720 --> 00:22:30.760
1 to 1 map of the me from the repo.

506
00:22:30.760 --> 00:22:31.880
And so there's no drift.

507
00:22:31.880 --> 00:22:34.440
So what my agents are reading, what their managers are reading

508
00:22:34.440 --> 00:22:37.120
is all the same content and it's all maintained in one place.

509
00:22:37.120 --> 00:22:39.920
And that was really just a very productive unlock.

510
00:22:39.920 --> 00:22:41.560
And it worked really well.

511
00:22:41.560 --> 00:22:44.320
And so the cultural shift that I really have to

512
00:22:44.320 --> 00:22:47.120
instill in my team was asking first, is this a skill?

513
00:22:47.120 --> 00:22:47.520
Right.

514
00:22:47.520 --> 00:22:51.080
So someone asks WebEx message like, hey,

