00:23:14.040 --> 00:23:17.240
now that we're operating at is like, hey, does anyone have a skill for this?

526
00:23:17.280 --> 00:23:20.160
If not, we create one together and we maintain it together.

527
00:23:20.160 --> 00:23:24.520
Again, I don't want 15 engineers creating 15 skills for the same thing,

528
00:23:24.560 --> 00:23:27.840
especially with this world of the token budget becoming a problem.

529
00:23:27.920 --> 00:23:30.200
That's just extremely wasteful engineering, right?

530
00:23:30.200 --> 00:23:32.360
We should all be trying to share when we can.

531
00:23:32.360 --> 00:23:33.360
We have coding agents.

532
00:23:33.360 --> 00:23:33.960
There's no reason

533
00:23:33.960 --> 00:23:37.240
that we can't really all work together and have our agents maintain it.

534
00:23:37.280 --> 00:23:39.960
As long as we have evals that define what the behavior should be.

535
00:23:39.960 --> 00:23:42.040
This is actually much easier than it sounds.

536
00:23:43.320 --> 00:23:43.600
Okay,

